u`. Só **um** módulo importa o PS.dll: - `wzAudiao.dll` (arquivo com typo) → importa **exatamente 1 função** do PS.dll: `wzAudioPlay` Os dois builds da DLL de áudio (`wzAudio.dll` e `wzAudiao.dll`) exportam as **mesmas 17 funções**. A diferença: - `wzAudio.dll` (limpo) → implementa `wzAudioPlay` internamente, **não precisa** de PS.dll - `wzAudiao.dll` (typo) → **encaminha** `wzAudioPlay` para o PS.dll → sem ele, o loader aborta com *\"PS.dll was not found\"* Nenhum módulo do jogo referencia o typo `wzAudiao` — todos carregam `wzAudio.dll`. Então, dependendo de qual conteúdo está no arquivo carregado, o erro aparecia. ## Solução: stub do PS.dll Criei um **PS.dll stub** (32-bit) que exporta `wzAudioPlay` como no-op. Isso satisfaz o loader em **qualquer** cenário, sem modificar nenhum arquivo original: - `F:\\blackrockmu\\PS.dll` ← o stub (82.944 bytes) - `PS_stub.cpp` / `PS_stub.def` / `build_ps.bat` ← fonte + rebuild **Convenção de chamada: cdecl** — confirmei desmontando o `wzAudioPlay` do `wzAudio.dll` (termina em `ret`/`0xC3` nos dois caminhos, sem imediato). ## Verificação (test_load.exe, 32-bit) ``` OK: LoadLibrary(wzAudiao.dll) handle=10000000 OK: PS.dll loaded handle=6C7B0000 OK: PS.dll!wzAudioPlay = 6C7B1010 OK: stack canary after call = 0x12345678 (expect 0x12345678) ``` - O `wzAudiao.dll` **carrega com sucesso** (antes falhava …\n- **Tools:** write_file, edit_file, mcp_tool, manage_todos, list_directory, read_file, run_command","vector":[0.07975797,0.042078655,-0.09765974,-0.031596188,0.017257653,-0.07243086,-0.002063836,0.03971431,-0.06882369,-0.04504398,-0.0134184845,0.023575667,0.09132327,-0.020363461,-0.010087812,-0.027111659,0.015058678,-0.08439025,-0.065911636,-0.010872059,0.025788398,-0.033685908,-0.04007992,-0.042947307,0.11077537,0.039209977,0.0016280632,0.05232476,-0.07393624,0.029118853,0.032394297,0.026104601,0.02464835,-0.0018391585,0.031478237,-0.053473093,0.041914757,-0.004185412,-0.013165675,0.033076506,-0.048930414,-0.04157779,-0.017251566,