) | ⚠️ acertava o monstro **vizinho** | **Prova (24 capturas nativas do `byp_packets.log`):** decifrei todas com XorData — em **todas** D2 = `0x78` (então o 0x78 é constante mesmo, em 4 alvos diferentes e 4 direções) e D0D1 = o índice **puro** do tracker (`00 1A`, `00 1B`, `00 25`, `00 5A`). O log do bot às 18:18 mostra o injetado enviando `EF EF` para o mesmo monstro `0x001A` que o nativo atingiu com `00 1A`. Isso também explica o \"antes atacava alguns monstros\": o DLL antigo acertava a entidade **adjacente** (24 em vez de 26) — em spawn denso era outro monstro vivo, então \"parecia funcionar\". ## Correções aplicadas 1. **`AttackModule.cpp` `BuildAttackPacket`**: D0D1 = `entityIndex` **puro** (removido o `EntityToAttackId`/XOR 0xEFF5 — essa convenção é do skill 0x19, não do 0x11) 2. **`AttackModule.cpp:188`**: `outBuf[5] = 0x78` — resolve o erro `C3861: ComputeActionByte not found` que você viu (a função tinha sido removid…\n- **Tools:** read_file, search_files, git, edit_file","vector":[0.040687945,0.075456806,-0.15193723,-0.017357172,0.07489392,-0.06707196,0.0396419,0.00613592,-0.06773409,-0.043706115,-0.08263833,0.024468737,0.06713828,-0.0012243558,0.014208592,-0.020219456,-0.012041747,-0.04787237,-0.044725753,0.04346383,0.036494143,-0.008090515,-0.0066002533,-0.03239751,0.05747077,0.04778117,0.007029196,0.07185658,-0.02962924,0.0008278968,0.024476329,0.055838153,-0.018160911,-0.012618829,0.0072114496,-0.042208306,0.036661237,0.009692332,-0.012794282,-0.009811172,-0.0051559242,-0.057798516,-0.0165102,0.016443988,0.016408753,0.037586283,0.05923846,0.039772425,0.045418452,-0.06641139,0.04972767,0.03477965,0.022266315,-0.041533273,0.09712949,0.044486873,-0.053196173,0.0055433847,0.044261232,-0.01646881,0.09716749,0.0061664945,0.010564657,0.06717274,-0.017908355,-0.040198643,-0.04433857,0.023661371,-0.0074232295,-0.010378281,0.048694097,0.00273204,0.011246779,0.019573472,0.0029936505,0.02450145,-0.008204837,-0.051016133,-0.047003344,-0.018509012,0.007211178,0.001